# Opt-in example for issue #14. NEVER included or installed automatically.
# These two directives are an EXAMPLE for the EXISTING, operator-approved
# /debian/ proxy location{} on an HTTPS server; not a new location or route.
# Change the constant label to the EXACT approved canonical location prefix
# for each repository. Never use untrusted request/header/submission input.
#
# If an access_log is inherited from http/server scope, setting this directive
# changes inheritance. Preserve any existing required site/access/audit logging
# explicitly under the same location after reviewing the effective config.
# Do not add this to repository-request intake or authentication endpoints.
set $repocache_metric_repo "/debian/";
access_log /var/log/nginx/repocache-metrics.log repocache_metrics;
